From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: GetNumberFormat of zero without a leading zero

Purpose: show "0 個の項目" ("0 items") in Windows 7's folder windows.
Windows behavior: GetNumberFormatW gives "0" for a zero value with no
decimals even when LeadingZero is 0 ("0", "0.0", "00"), and a value that
shows as zero has no negative sign ("-0" gives "0", or ".00" with two
decimals). Measured on Windows 7 (tests/number-format.c).
Wine before: "" for zero with LeadingZero 0 and no decimals, and "-",
"-0" for negative zero. Windows 7's shell formats the item count with
such a format, so an empty folder's details pane said " 個の項目".
Change: format_number shows a 0 when nothing else is shown;
get_number_format drops the sign of a value shown as zero.
Evidence: the test's output is the same as Windows 7's; the empty
folder's details pane matches.
Scope: all programs (as on Windows).
---
 dlls/kernelbase/locale.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/locale.c b/dlls/kernelbase/locale.c
index 75f018d..853cdae 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/locale.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/locale.c
@@ -7656,7 +7656,8 @@ static WCHAR *format_number( WCHAR *end, const WCHAR *value, const WCHAR *decima
         if (len) end = prepend_str( end, thousand_sep );
     }
     if (round) *(--end) = '1';
-    else if (lzero) *(--end) = '0';
+    /* nothing else to show: Windows shows 0 even without a leading zero */
+    else if (lzero || !*end) *(--end) = '0';
     return end;
 }
 
@@ -7717,6 +7718,9 @@ static int get_number_format( const NLS_LOCALE_DATA *locale, DWORD flags, const
         return 0;
     }
 
+    /* a value that shows as zero has no sign */
+    if (negative && !num[wcscspn( num, L"123456789" )]) negative = FALSE;
+
     if (negative)
     {
         switch (order)
